    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d473">

                <pb facs="0682" n="594" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg594"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Foster to Mr. Newberry.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-09-16"><hi rendition="#italic">September 16,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 386.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    Nos. 521, 522, 524, and 525 of the 24th, 25th, and 27th ultimos, in further
                    relation to the case of Mr. Bartlett at Bourdour.</p>
                <p>It affords me pleasure to commend the zeal with which you have pressed our just
                    claim in the premises to a conclusion, in execution of the telegraphic
                    instructions of this Department.</p>
                <p>The matter of a pecuniary payment by way of reparation for the actual loss
                    sustained and personal indemnity for Mr. Bartlett, appears to remove this phase
                    of the question from the field of diplomatic action. It is trusted that the
                    sense of justice and friendly disposition of the Turkish Government will not
                    halt here, but that its efforts will be continued in the directions outlined by
                    your presentation of the demands of this Government; and that not only will Mr.
                    Bartlett receive the positive measure of protection due and promised, but that
                    the displeasure of the Ottoman Government will be signally visited upon the
                    perpetrators of the wrong and upon the dependents of its authority <pb
                        facs="0683" n="595" xml:id="pg595"/> whose negligence or inefficiency may
                    have contributed to bring about this regrettable incident.</p>
                <p>Awaiting your further report as to the manner in which the payment of the
                    indemnity was effected,</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John. W. Foster.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
